# Installed as `.gitattributes`. If this project already had one, adoption
# wrote this alongside it instead of overwriting — merge the rule below in.
#
# This matters because adoption may install `.githooks/pre-push`, a `#!/bin/sh`
# script. A stale CRLF working file is a portability hazard: the effect
# depends on the platform and the shell. The framework observed macOS Git
# refuse such a hook with `cannot exec ... No such file or directory`, while
# tested Windows Git for Windows plus its bundled GNU bash executed the hook's
# real logic. Other Windows shells and WSL/Cygwin Git were not tested.
#
# `eol=lf`, not bare `text=auto`: `text=auto` alone normalises to LF in the
# repository but still checks out CRLF on Windows, which is the case that
# breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf
